commit 66ee9999011ed557510ddd18f20ceca6cb4aa5ae
Author: Jarod Castillo <43973221+Smotto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Tue Nov 3 00:43:49 2026 +0000

    psi: query validation's expression intervals at use, not as flow facts (#1582)
    
    Stage 05 flow copied validation's arithmetic intervals onto every
    completed integer value as `AssignedIntegerBounds` facts and carried them
    with the value. Checks then read the copies back. Flow no longer copies
    them. The two checks that needed them now ask the interval engine about
    the exact expression at the point of use, and every stage-05 interval read
    goes through one query.
    
    Before, `checking.rs` passed validation's interval slice through flow's
    builder and context, the range checks, call contracts and
    captured-boolean proofs (12 signatures). Each reader searched it with
    `validation::expression_interval(slice, expression)`. Now the slice is
    attached once to the checking context, like the storage graph, and
    `CheckingInput::expression_interval(expression)` answers. The parameters
    are gone.
    
    Which readers moved off the flow copy:
    - An exit `ensures result >= c` reads the returned operand's own
      enclosure (`ExpressionInterval::carrier_range`), intersected with any
      bounds still published on that place
      (exits/scalars/result_bounds.rs).
    - A runtime index selector narrows to a fixed element when its own
      enclosure is one value (flow/place/canonicalization.rs). This keeps the
      write to `items[index]` from expiring facts about `items[0]` when
      `index` is known to be 1.
    
    This is the first input that flow stops copying from validation (deep
    A4). Exact casts, integer-assignment decisions and float projections
    remain.
    
    Validation:
    - Witnesses identified by a knockout that withheld only the intervals
      from flow: 4 of the 32 A4 witnesses failed (three `result >= c` exit
      places and `indexed_domain_known_disjoint_call_exit`). 0 of the
      150-fixture A4 sample failed. All 4 pass with this change.
    - The same 4, the other 28 A4 witnesses and 118 index, window, length,
      rank and termination fixtures (150 in all, 33 that must reject) were
      checked with the previous commit and with this one: identical outcomes.

